                and of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivariant+K-theory"} equivariant K-theory
                (hence of
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+equivariant+K-theory"} twisted equivariant K-theory
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sections"} sections
                of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Fred
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fred(\mathscr{H})
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+bundles"} fiber bundles
                (
                %a{:href => "#AtiyahSegal04"}> Atiyah &amp; Segal 2004
                ).
          %h2#Statement Statement
          %p
            The original Atiyah-Jänich theorem theorem concerns complex
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mi KU
                    %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(-) = KU^0(-)
            in degree 0 (and hence in any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/even+number"} even
            degree), see:
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#StatementForKU0"}>
                Statement for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %msup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \mathrm{U}^0
              \.
          %p
            Generalization to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO-theory"} KO-theory
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KSp-theory"} KSp-theory
            in degree 0 is fairly straightforward by just replacing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#StatementForKO0andKSp0"}>
                Statement for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %msup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \mathrm{O}^0
                and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %msup
                        %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                        %mn 4
                      %mo =
                      %mi K
                      %msup
                        %mi Sp
                        %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \mathrm{O}^4 = K Sp^0
              \.
          %p
            Generalization to any degree over any ground field is due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AtiyahSinger1969"} Atiyah &amp; Singer 1969
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Karoubi1970"} Karoubi 1970
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#StatementForKU1"}>
                  Statement for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi KU
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KU^1
                \.
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#StatementForKO2andKO6"}
                  Statement for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %msup
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                          %mrow
                            %mo ±
                            %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \mathrm{O}^{\pm 2}
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#StatementForKO1andKO7"}
                  Statement for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %msup
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                          %mrow
                            %mo ±
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \mathrm{O}^{\pm 1}
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "#StatementForKO3andKO5"}
                  Statement for
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                        %msup
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                          %mrow
                            %mo ±
                            %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \mathrm{O}^{\pm 3}
          %p
            In stating these, we mostly review results from
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#[Karoubi1970](#Karoubi1970"} Karoubi 1970 §I
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#SatiSchreiber2023"} Sati &amp; Schreiber 2023 §2.2
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/10-fold+way"} 10-fold way
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+symmetries"} quantum symmetries
            as known from the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+topological+phases+of+matter"} K-theory classification of topological phases of matter
          %h3#StatementForKU0
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \mathrm{U}^0
          %p
            Let
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+operator"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fred
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fred(\mathscr{H})
            denote the space of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+operators"} Fredholm operators
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm+topology"} norm topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
          %blockquote
            %p
              (A more ambitious construction modifies
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Fred
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fred(\mathscr{H})
              up to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalence
              to have it carry a continuous action of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PU%28%E2%84%8B%29"} PU(ℋ)
              with the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operator+topology"} operator topology
          %p
          #KernelBundles.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Fred
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Fred(\mathscr{H})
              is such that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+vector+space"} dimension
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernels"} kernels
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x)
              is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+constant+function"} locally constant
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/integers"} integers
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    dim\Big(
                    ker\big(
                    f(-)
                    \\big)
                    \\Big)
                    \\,\colon\,
                    X \longrightarrow \mathbb{Z}
            %p
              then the collection of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernels"} kernels
              and
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cokernels"} cokernels
              themselves, as
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspaces"} subspaces
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                      %mo ×
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times \mathscr{H}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+vector+bundles"} topological vector bundles
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi coker
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℂ
                    %msub
                      %mi Vec
                      %mi X
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    ker\big(
                    f(-)
                    \\big),
                    \\;
                    coker\big(
                    f(-)
                    \\big)
                    \\in
                    \\mathbb{C}Vec_{X}
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Jänich65"}> Jänich 1965 Lemma 4
            ).
          %p
          #ConstantKernelDeformationsExist.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Fred
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon X \longrightarrow Fred(\mathscr{H})
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopic
              to a map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
              for which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dim
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim\big(ker(f')\big)
              is continuous.
          (
          %a{:href => "#Jänich65"}> Jänich 1965 below Lemma 4 using Lemma 3
          ).
          %p
          #IndexViaVirtualKernelBundlesOfConstantDimPerturbation.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The index
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:IndexMap"} (1)
              is given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi π
                            %mn 0
                          %mi Map
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Fred
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi ind
                                %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mi K
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} [
                          %mi ker
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊖
                          %mi coker
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi f
                          %mo ′
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ]
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{ccc}
                    \\pi_0 Map\big(X,Fred(\mathscr{H})\big)
                    \&amp;\xrightarrow{ ind_X }&amp;
                    K(X)
                    \\\
                    [f]
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    \\big[ker(f') \ominus coker(f')\big]
                    \\mathrlap{\,,}
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'
              is any representative of the class
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [f]
              according to Prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ConstantKernelDeformationsExist"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ker(f')
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi coker
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} coker(f')
              are its (co)kernel bundles according to Prop.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KernelBundles"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊖
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-) \ominus (-)
              is their their
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/virtual+vector+bundle"} virtual difference bundle
          (
          %a{:href => "#Jänich65"}> Jänich 1965 Lemma 5
          )
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              The construction of the index map
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:IndexMap"} (1)
              by
              %a{:href => "#Atiyah67"} Atiyah 1967 Lem A3, Cor A4
              is a little different (though the result, of course, is the same). Exposition is in
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#Sheth"} Sheth §2
          %p
          #TheSpaceOfGradedFredholmOperators.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              %strong (Graded Fredholm operators)
              %br/
              It turns out to be useful (such as for the discussion of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/twisted+equivariant+K-theory"} twisted equivariant K-theory
              and of the
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/K-theory+classification+of+topological+phases+of+matter"} K-theory classification of topological phases of matter
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "Fredholm+operator#AtiyahSegal04"} Atiyah &amp; Segal 2004 Def. 3.2
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#AtiyahSinger69"} Atiyah &amp; Singer 1969 p 7
              %a{:href => "Fredholm+operator#FredZero"} here
              at
              = succeed "):" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+operator"} Fredholm operator
            %p
              Given any
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cyclic+group+of+order+2"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded
              infinite-dimensional (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/separable+Hilbert+space"} separable
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+space"} complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %mi gr
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %mo +
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %mo −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathscr{H}_{gr}
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\mathscr{H}_+ \oplus \mathscr{H}_-
            %p write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Fred
                      %mi gr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %mi gr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %mi gr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Fred_{gr}(\mathscr{H}_{gr})
                    \\;\subset\;
                    \\mathcal{B}(\mathscr{H}_{gr})
            %p
              for the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bounded+linear+operators"} bounded linear operators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo →
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \,\colon\, \mathscr{H} \to \mathscr{H}
              which are
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-adjoint+operator"}> self-adjoint
                  \:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi F
                            %mo †
                          %mo =
                          %mi F
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F^\dagger = F
              %li
                %p
                  odd-graded:
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mo ±
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊂
                          %msub
                            %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mo ∓
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(\mathscr{H}_{\pm}) \subset \mathscr{H}_{\mp}
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+operator"} Fredholm
                  in that there exists such
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi F
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ˜
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \tilde F
                  which is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parametrix"} parametrix
            %p
              equipped with the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/norm+topology"} norm topology
            %p
              This just means that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Fred
                      %mi gr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %mi gr
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \in Fred_{gr}(\mathscr{H}_{gr})
              is of the form
            #eq:GradedFredholmOperatorInComponents.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %msup
                                %mi f
                                %mo †
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi f
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi End
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %mo +
                    %mo ⊕
                    %msub
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F
                    \\;=\;
                    \\left(
                    \\begin{matrix}
                    0 &amp; f^\dagger
                    \\\
                    f &amp; 0
                    \\end{matrix}
                    \\right)
                    \\;\in\;
                    End\big(
                    \\mathscr{H}_+ \oplus \mathscr{H}_-
                    \\big)
            %p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              an ordinary
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+operator"} Fredholm operator
            %p
              Therefore this space is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
              to the standard space of Fredholm operators:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Fred
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi.mathscript ℋ
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo ⟶
                            %mo ∼
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi Fred
                            %mi gr
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi.mathscript ℋ
                            %mi gr
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mrow
                              %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %mn 0
                                  %mtd
                                    %msup
                                      %mi f
                                      %mo †
                                %mtr
                                  %mtd
                                    %mi f
                                  %mtd
                                    %mn 0
                            %mo )
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{ccc}
                    Fred(\mathscr{H})
                    \&amp;\overset{\sim}{\longrightarrow}&amp;
                    Fred_gr(\mathscr{H}_{gr})
                    \\\
                    f
                    \&amp;\mapsto&amp;
                    \\left(
                    \\begin{matrix}
                    0 &amp; f^\dagger
                    \\\
                    f &amp; 0
                    \\end{matrix}
                    \\right)
                    \\mathrlap{\,,}
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              but the way it is presented by graded operators makes manifest that there is “charge conjugation”
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+symmetry"} quantum symmetry
              acting on this space, namely by swapping the two homogeneously graded Hilbert space summands. This is useful in the following for neatly expressing (anti-)self-adjointness conditions on Fredholm operators.
            %p
              (The point of
              %a{:href => "Fredholm+operator#AtiyahSegal04"} Atiyah &amp; Segal 2004 §4
              is to further modify this space so that it carries a non-contractible
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact-open+topology"} compact-open topology
              which allows for more general
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PU%28%E2%84%8B%29"} PU(ℋ)
              actions on it. The commutation relations discussed in the following immediately apply also to this modified space and constrain the components
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              of its elements
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              in the same way. It seems plausible that the correspondingly constrained modified spaces are accordingly classifying spaces for the various flavors of K-theory as is the case for the unmodified space — as summarized
              %a{:href => "#SummaryInTermsOfGradedFredholmOperators"} below
              — but this is not actually obvious.)
          %h3#StatementForKU1
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} U
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \mathrm{U}^1
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              The space of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-adjoint+operator"} self-adjoint
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+operators"} Fredholm operators
            #eq:SpaceOfSelfAdjointFredholmOperators.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Fred
                      %mi sa
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} {
                    %mi f
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Fred
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo †
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Fred^{sa}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\subset
                    \\Big\{
                    f \in Fred
                    \\;\Big\vert\;
                    f^\dagger = f
                    \\Big\}
            %p
              has three
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Fred
                      %mi sa
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Fred
                      %mo +
                      %mi sa
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Fred
                      %mo −
                      %mi sa
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Fred
                      %mo *
                      %mi sa
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Fred^{sa}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    Fred_+^{sa}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\,\sqcup\,
                    Fred_-^{sa}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\,\sqcup\,
                    Fred_\ast^{sa}(\mathscr{H})
                    \\mathrlap{\,,}
            %p
              corresponding to those Fredholm operators whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essential+spectrum"} essential spectrum
              (which is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-adjoint+operator"} self-adjointness
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Fred
                          %mo +
                          %mi sa
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fred_+^{sa}(\mathscr{H})
                  \: purely
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+number"} positive
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Fred
                          %mo −
                          %mi sa
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fred_-^{sa}(\mathscr{H})
                  \: purely
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negative+number"} negative
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Fred
                          %mo *
                          %mi sa
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fred_{\ast}^{sa}(\mathscr{H})
                  \: both, hence
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} nonempty
                  both above and below
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/zero"} zero
            %p Moreover,
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  the first two components are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible+topological+space"} contractible
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Fred
                          %mo ±
                          %mi sa
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi.mathscript ℋ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mo *
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Fred^{sa}_{\pm}(\mathscr{H}) \simeq \ast
                        \\,,
              %li
                %p
                  the last component is
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotoppy equivalent
                  to the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+unitary+group"} stable unitary group
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
                  for
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+K-theory"} topological K-theory
                  in odd degree:
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Fred
                          %mo *
                          %mi sa
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi U
                        %mo ≃
                        %msub
                          %mi KU
                          %mn 1
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        Fred^{sa}_{\ast} \simeq U \simeq KU_1
                        \\,.
            %p
          %p
            Up to some straightforward re-identifications (for instance one may equivalently use
            %em skew
            self-adjoint operators whose spectrum is then purely
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/imaginary+number"} imaginary
            %a{:href => "#AtiyahSinger1969"} Atiyah &amp; Singer 1969 Thm. B
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Karoubi1970"} Karoubi 1970 Lem 1.4 &amp; Prop. 1.5
          %p
          #SelfAdjointViaCommutingWithP.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              In terms of the graded Fredholm operators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GradedFredholmOperatorInComponents"} (2)
              from Rem.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TheSpaceOfGradedFredholmOperators"}
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SpaceOfSelfAdjointFredholmOperators"} (8)
              are equivalently those that commute with the operator
            #eq:TheChargeSwappingOperator.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi P
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mrow
                        %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mi id
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi id
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\widehat{P}
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    \\begin{matrix}
                    0 &amp; id
                    \\\
                    id &amp; 0
                    \\end{matrix}
                    \\right)
                    \\,.
            %p
          %h3#StatementForKO0andKSp0
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \mathrm{O}^0
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                    %mn 4
                  %mo =
                  %mi K
                  %msup
                    %mi Sp
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \mathrm{O}^4 = K Sp^0
          %p
            The directly analogous discussion as for complex K-theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi KU
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} KU^0
            in degree 0 (
            %a{:href => "#StatementForKU0"}> above
            ) applies when replacing the underlying complex Hilbert space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
            with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+vector+space"} real
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+vector+space"} quaternionic
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO-theory"} KO-theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+K-theory"} quaternionic K-theory
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KSp-theory"}> KSp-theory
            ) in degree=0, respectively.
          %p
            It is useful to express this in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+vector+spaces"} complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+spaces"} Hilbert spaces
            but equipped with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+structure"} real structure
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+structure"} quaternionic structure
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antilinear+map"} antilinear map
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi T
                    %mo ^
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi.mathscript ℋ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\widehat{T}
                  \\,\colon\,
                  \\mathscr{H} \longrightarrow \mathscr{H}
          %p
            which squares to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ±
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm 1
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi T
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat T
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antilinear+map"} antilinear map
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi T
                        %mo ^
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mi id
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\widehat T^2 = + id
                    \\mathrlap{\,,}
            %p
              then the space of
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+operators"} Fredholm operators
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Fred
                      %mi ℝ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} {
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Fred
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∘
                    %mover
                      %mi T
                      %mo ^
                    %mo =
                    %mover
                      %mi T
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                    %mi O
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi KO
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Fred_{\mathbb{R}}
                    \\,\coloneqq\,
                    \\Big\{
                    F \in Fred
                    \\,\Big\vert\,
                    F \circ \widehat T
                    \=
                    \\widehat{T} \circ F
                    \\Big\}
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    B O
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    KO_0
            %p
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalent
              to the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+orthogonal+group"} stable orthogonal group
              and hence is a classifying space for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KO-theory"} KO-theory
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Jänich65"}> Jänich 1965 p. 132
            ;
            = succeed ";" do
              %a{:href => "#Atiyah69"} Atiyah 1969 §2 p. 102
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Karoubi1970"} Karoubi 1970 Prop. 1.3 p. 78
          %p
          .num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              %br>/
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi T
                      %mo ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat T
              be an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antilinear+map"} antilinear map
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi.mathscript ℋ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
              such that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mover
                        %mi T
                        %mo ^
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi id
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\widehat T^2 = - id
                    \\mathrlap{\,,}
            %p
              then the space of
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternionic
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fredholm+operators"} Fredholm operators
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Fred
                      %mi ℍ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} {
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Fred
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi F
                    %mo ∘
                    %mover
                      %mi T
                      %mo ^
                    %mo =
                    %mover
                      %mi T
                      %mo ^
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi B
                    %mi Sp
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi KO
                      %mn 4
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Fred_{\mathbb{H}}
                    \\,\coloneqq\,
                    \\Big\{
                    F \in Fred
                    \\,\Big\vert\,
                    F \circ \widehat T
                    \=
                    \\widehat{T} \circ F
                    \\Big\}
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    B Sp
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    KO_4
            %p
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+equivalence"} homotopy equivalent
              to the
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              of the stable
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+unitary+group"} quaternionic unitary group
              and hence is a classifying space for
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KSp-theory"} KSp-theory
            %p
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#AtiyahSinger1969"}> Atiyah &amp; Singer 1969 p. 323
            ;
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Karoubi1970"} Karoubi 1970 Prop. 1.12 p. 81
          %h3#StatementForKO2andKO6
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %msup
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} O
                    %mrow
                      %mo ±
                      %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \mathrm{O}^{\pm 2}
          %p First some basic preliminaries:
          %p
          #SelfAdjointAntiLinearOperator.num_lemma
            %h6 Lemma
            %p
              For a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-linear+operator"} anti-linear operator
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hilbert+space"} Hilbert space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi.mathscript ℋ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathscr{H}
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  is Hermitian self-adjoint,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mo †
                          %mo =
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^\dagger = A
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "antilinear+map#DefinitionOnHermitianSpaces"} there
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+inner+product"} Hermitian inner product
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle -,-\rangle
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                  is
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/self-adjoint+operator"} self-adjoint
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi A
                            %mo *
                          %mo =
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^\ast = A
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+operator"} linear operator
                  with respect to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/underlying"} underlying
                  real inner product,
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi Re
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Re\big(\langle -,-\rangle\big)
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+part"} real part
                  of the
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+inner+product"} Hermitian inner product
            %p
          .proof
            %h6 Proof
            %p One direction is immediate:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                    %mi A
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                    %mo =
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                        %mi v
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mi w
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                      %mo ¯
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Re
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                    %mi A
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Re
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %mover
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                        %mi v
                        %mo ,
                        %mi A
                        %mi w
                        %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Re
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\big\langle A v , w \big\rangle
                    \=
                    \\overline{
                    \\big\langle v , A w \big\rangle
                    }
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    \\Rightarrow
                    \\;\;\;\;\;\;
                    Re\Big(
                    \\big\langle A v , w \big\rangle
                    \\Big)
                    \=
                    Re\Big(
                    \\overline{
                    \\big\langle v , A w \big\rangle
                    }
                    \\Big)
                    \=
                    Re\Big(
                    \\big\langle v , A w \big\rangle
                    \\Big)
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
            %p In the other direction: Assuming that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Re
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                    %mi A
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi Re
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Re\Big(
                    \\big\langle A v , w \big\rangle
                    \\Big)
                    \=
                    Re\Big(
                    \\big\langle v , A w \big\rangle
                    \\Big)
            %p we need to show that then
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Im
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                    %mi A
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi Im
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                    %mi v
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mi w
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                    %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Im\Big(
                    \\big\langle A v , w \big\rangle
                    \\Big)
                    \=
                    \-
                    Im\Big(
                    \\big\langle v , A w \big\rangle
                    \\Big)
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
            %p
              For that we compute as follows (where we use the convention that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle-,-\rangle
              is anti-linear in the first and linear in the second argument, but the same conclusion holds of course with the other convention):
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "left left left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi Im
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                          %mi A
                          %mi v
                          %mo ,
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi Re
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                          %mi A
                          %mi v
                          %mo ,
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mtext basic property of complex arithmetic
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi Re
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                          %mi A
                          %mi v
                          %mo ,
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mtext sesqui-linearity of inner product
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi Re
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                          %mi v
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mtext assumption of real self-adjointness
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi Re
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                          %mi v
                          %mo ,
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                          %mi A
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mtext assumption of complex anti-linearity
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi Re
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} i
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                          %mi v
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mtext sesqui-linearity of inner product
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mi Im
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} (
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                          %mi v
                          %mo ,
                          %mi A
                          %mi w
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                          %mo{:maxsize => "1.8em", :minsize => "1.8em"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mtext basic property of complex arithmetic
                          %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                              %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{lll}
                    Im\Big(
                    \\big\langle A v , w \big\rangle
                    \\Big)
                    \&amp; =
                    Re\Big(
                    \-\mathrm{i}
                    \\big\langle A v , w \big\rangle
                    \\Big)
                    \&amp; \text{basic property of complex arithmetic}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Re\Big(
                    \\big\langle A v , - \mathrm{i} w \big\rangle
                    \\Big)
                    \&amp; \text{sesqui-linearity of inner product}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Re\Big(
                    \\big\langle v , A(-\mathrm{i} w) \big\rangle
                    \\Big)
                    \&amp; \text{assumption of real self-adjointness}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Re\Big(
                    \\big\langle v , \mathrm{i} A w \big\rangle
                    \\Big)
                    \&amp; \text{assumption of complex anti-linearity}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    Re\Big(
                    \\mathrm{i}
                    \\big\langle v , A w \big\rangle
                    \\Big)
                    \&amp; \text{sesqui-linearity of inner product}
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \-Im\Big(
                    \\big\langle v , A w \big\rangle
                    \\Big)
                    \&amp; \text{basic property of complex arithmetic}
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
                    \\end{array}
            %p
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+structure"} real structure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℂ
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mover
                                %mi T
                                %mo ^
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %mi ℂ
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi z
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mi z
                            %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{ccc}
                    \\mathbb{C}
                    \&amp;\xrightarrow{\; \widehat{T} \;}&amp;
                    \\mathbb{C}
                    \\\
                    z &amp;\mapsto&amp; \overline{z}
                    \\end{array}
            %p
              is self-adjoint (cf. Lem.
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SelfAdjointAntiLinearOperator"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                            %mover
                              %mi T
                              %mo ^
                            %mi z
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                            %mover
                              %mi z
                              %mo ¯
                            %mo ,
                            %mi w
                            %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mover
                              %mover
                                %mi z
                                %mo ¯
                              %mo ¯
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi w
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mi z
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mi w
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %mover
                                  %mi z
                                  %mo ¯
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mover
                                  %mi w
                                  %mo ¯
                              %mo ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                                %mi z
                                %mo ,
                                %mover
                                  %mi w
                                  %mo ¯
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                              %mo ¯
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %mover
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟨
                                %mi z
                                %mo ,
                                %mover
                                  %mi T
                                  %mo ^
                                %mi w
                                %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} ⟩
                              %mo ¯
                            %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                              %mrow
                                %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                                %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    \\big\langle
                    \\widehat{T} z
                    ,
                    w
                    \\big\rangle
                    \&amp; =
                    \\big\langle
                    \\overline{z}
                    ,
                    w
                    \\big\rangle
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\overline{\overline{z}} \, w
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    z \, w
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\overline{
                    \\overline{z} \, \overline{w}
                    }
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\overline{
                    \\big\langle
                    z, \overline{w}
                    \\big\rangle
                    }
                    \\\
                    \&amp; =
                    \\overline{
                    \\big\langle
                    z, \widehat{T} w
                    \\big\rangle
                    }
                    \\mathrlap{\,.}
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternionic+structure"} quaternionic structure
              on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℂ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^2
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ℂ
                            %mn 2
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mover
                                %mi T
                                %mo ^
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi ℂ
                            %mn 2
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mrow
                            %mo (
                            %mrow
                              %mtable{:displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                                %mtr
